.TH TGLFS 1 "July 2026" "tglfs 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tglfs \- authenticate with Telegram, manage TGLFS files, transfer files, and create previewable MP4 copies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tglfs
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-interactive
Disable interactive prompts and fail instead of prompting.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tglfs
is a global command-line client for authenticating with Telegram, uploading files, managing TGLFS file cards, transferring files between peers, searching mailboxes, converting stored MP4 files for streaming Preview, and downloading current-format or legacy TGLFS files by UFID.
.PP
Run
.B tglfs help <command>
for subcommand-specific help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B upload <paths...>
Upload one file, or archive multiple files, into Saved Messages.
.TP
.B login
Authenticate with Telegram and persist the resulting session.
.TP
.B status
Show current config and Telegram authorization state.
.TP
.B logout
Remove the saved Telegram session.
.TP
.B search [query]
Search TGLFS file cards in Saved Messages or another peer mailbox.
.TP
.B download <ufid>
Download a current-format or legacy TGLFS file by UFID.
.TP
.B make-previewable <ufid>
Create a new fragmented MP4 copy suitable for streaming Preview. Front-loaded MP4s are converted and uploaded as one bounded stream; trailing-metadata MP4s use a temporary source file. The original remains unchanged.
.TP
.B rename <ufid> <new-name>
Rename an owned TGLFS file card.
.TP
.B delete <ufid...>
Delete one or more owned TGLFS files.
.TP
.B send <ufid...> --to <peer>
Send one or more owned TGLFS files to another peer.
.TP
.B receive <source> <ufid...>
Receive one or more TGLFS files from another peer into Saved Messages.
.TP
.B unsend <source> <ufid...>
Delete one or more received TGLFS files from another peer mailbox.
.TP
.B inspect <ufid>
Inspect file-card metadata and chunk references; use
.B --probe
for a full current-vs-legacy integrity check.
.TP
.B sync <command>
Initialize, push, pull, list, and inspect folder sync roots backed by TGLFS sync manifests.
.TP
.B help [command]
Display help for a command.
.SH FILES
The CLI stores config and session files in OS-standard per-user app directories. Temporary MP4 source files are created only for inputs whose
.B moov
metadata follows media data and are removed after conversion.
